==Old Norse==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hleuzą||cheek, ear}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱlews-||temple of the forehead, cheek}}. More at {{l|en|leer}}.

====Noun====
{{non-noun|n}}

# [[cheek]]; [[face]]
# The sides (cheeks) of an [[axe]] blade, [[knife]], or [[bodice]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hliwjaz}}, {{term/t|gem-pro|*hlēwaz}}, {{term/t|gem-pro|*hlēwijaz||warm}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱal(w)e-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱel(w)e-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*k(')lēw-||warm, hot}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term/t|ang|hlēow||warm, sunny}}. More at {{l|en|lukewarm}}.

====Adjective====
{{non-adj}}

# [[warm]], [[mild]]

